# Logitech PRO WIRELESS (046d:4079 through its 046d:c539 receiver, 046d:c088
# cabled) -> uaccess on its own hidraw node through the receiver, and on its
# HID++ interface, 02, on its cable.
#
# Not yet checked on this hardware. Its receiver is a LIGHTSPEED one that the
# kernel's hid-logitech-dj binds as it binds the G305's, so the mouse gets a
# hidraw node of its own, matched by its HID device name as 70-g305.rules
# matches the G305's (libratbag issue 1875's log: product 0x4079 beside the
# receiver's 0xc539). A property match would also take in the receiver's
# interfaces. The c539 pairs one device (Solaar's listing: "a maximum of
# 1"), so no keyboard can share its node.
#
# The node still carries the keystrokes the mouse sends for a button its
# onboard profile binds to a key, as 70-g502x.rules says of the G502 X PLUS's.
#
# Cabled, its firmware's USB descriptors (MPM15.02_B0026) give 00 a boot
# mouse, 01 a keyboard and 02 the vendor collection, the G502 X PLUS's
# layout. Interface 01 is not granted.
#
# No event node is granted: in host mode Gearbench reads the buttons it binds
# through HID++ on the hidraw nodes below, and outside host mode none.
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", KERNELS=="0003:046D:4079.*", TAG+="uaccess"
KERNEL=="hidraw*", SUBSYSTEM=="hidraw", ENV{ID_VENDOR_ID}=="046d", ENV{ID_MODEL_ID}=="c088", ENV{ID_USB_INTERFACE_NUM}=="02", TAG+="uaccess"
